IN THE COURT OF THE LEARNED CIVIL JUDGE / ADDITIONAL DISTRICT JUDGE, UDAIPUR

Civil Suit No. ______ of 2025

Smt. Kamla Devi                                                          … Plaintiff

Versus

Shri Vikram Singh                                                        … Defendant

JUDGMENT
(Draft – Decree for Permanent Injunction)

1. This is a suit for permanent injunction restraining the Defendant from interfering with the Plaintiff’s possession of House No. 22, Patel Nagar, Udaipur and from obstructing a 10-ft wide passage used as right of way / easement.

2. The Plaintiff’s case is that she is the owner in possession and has been using the passage for more than 20 years. The Defendant has started construction activity that will block the passage.

3. The Defendant denied the easement and claimed the strip belongs to him.

4. Issues framed included existence of right, interference, and entitlement to injunction.

5. Findings:
   - Plaintiff has proved ownership and peaceful possession.
   - Long user of the passage is established by oral and documentary evidence.
   - Defendant’s construction activity constitutes clear interference.
   - All three ingredients for injunction are satisfied.

6. Relief:
   The suit is decreed with costs.
   The Defendant, his agents and any person claiming through him are permanently restrained from interfering with the Plaintiff’s possession of House No. 22 and from obstructing, blocking or constructing any structure on or over the 10-ft wide passage described in Schedule-B of the plaint, and from interfering with the Plaintiff’s right of way, light and air.

Decree-sheet be prepared.

